# created: 2026-10-18 | branch: beta/k1a-gate0-harness | author: Larry Klosowski + Claude Opus 5.5 (MAC lane)
# status: active (SCL-S1.3 suite manifest; the SCL-S13.2 tripwire builds on it)
#
# The lifecycle fault-injection suite manifest. One line per fixture in kit/tests/lifecycle_faults.rs:
#   name | kind | work package | what it proves
# kind: harness (the harness itself), positive-control (green on the current supervisor and must
# stay green), regression (a fixed defect; failed first, in the PR that fixed it).
# Removing or #[ignore]-ing a listed fixture needs an ADR reference (Rule 2; enforced in SCL-S13.2).

harness_guard_cleans_up_after_a_panicking_body | harness | SCL-S1.3 | guard kills and reaps every recorded pid, reparented descendants included, when the body panics
harness_guard_never_signals_an_unmarked_pid | harness | SCL-S1.3 | a recorded pid without the marker is reported foreign and never signalled
harness_sweep_finds_marked_processes_missing_from_the_record | harness | SCL-S1.3 | a marked process missing from the pid file is still found and killed
harness_never_signals_pid_zero_or_a_wrapping_pid | harness | SCL-S2.2 | the harness refuses pid 0 and wrapping pids, so it never signals its own group or a negative pid
harness_unreaped_child_fails_the_reaped_check | harness | SCL-S1.3 | an exited child nobody waited for fails the reaped check and is reported left behind
harness_recorded_pids_are_killed_without_the_sweep | harness | SCL-S1.3 | with the sweep off, cleanup still kills every recorded marked pid, reparented descendants included
harness_pgrep_matches_the_marker_as_a_fixed_string | harness | SCL-S1.3 | the harness pgrep matches the marker as a fixed string: a `.` never matches another character
harness_timing_windows_are_monotonic_and_never_short | harness | SCL-S1.3 | waits and observation windows run on the monotonic clock and never end early
pc_fresh_start_creates_exactly_one_incarnation | positive-control | SCL-S1.3 | a fresh Start creates one incarnation and no other over 2 s (bug a positive half)
pc_single_stop_ends_the_child_and_stays_off | positive-control | SCL-S1.3 | one Stop ends and reaps the child; Off with no new child over 2 s
pc_crash_respawns_a_distinct_incarnation | positive-control | SCL-S1.3 | an external kill is a crash and yields one distinct new incarnation
pc_crash_loop_reaches_failed_after_the_retry_budget | positive-control | SCL-S1.3 | a crash loop runs once plus max_retries, then Failed, then nothing
pc_fixture_processes_carry_the_suite_prefix | harness | SCL-S1.3 | every fixture process is visible to the CI job's pgrep -f citrate-lcf- check
stop_in_off_never_respawns | regression | SCL-S2.2 | bug (a): a second Stop on a stopped service creates no child over 2 s
stop_in_backoff_never_respawns | regression | SCL-S2.2 | a Stop in Backoff cancels the retry; a second Stop changes nothing over 2 s
concurrent_stops_during_teardown_never_respawn | regression | SCL-S2.2 | 8 Stops racing one teardown leave one stopped service, no respawn over 2 s
repeated_stop_joins_receipt | regression | SCL-S2.2 | a repeated Stop joins the first receipt; Accepted is Pending until Complete; Stop when stopped is AlreadySatisfied
explicit_start_after_stop_creates_exactly_one_incarnation | positive-control | SCL-S2.2 | one explicit Start after Stop creates exactly one new incarnation
stop_with_a_held_reader_is_incomplete_and_quarantined | regression | SCL-S2.2 | a reader held open makes Stop Incomplete and the service Quarantined until it really ends
start_during_held_reader_teardown_waits_for_cleanup | regression | SCL-S2.2 | a Start that supersedes a Stop mid-teardown spawns nothing until the old incarnation's readers are reconciled
stop_without_a_monitor_is_observation_unknown | regression | SCL-S2.2 | with the monitor gone, every Stop and Start (repeated or joining) is ObservationUnknown, never Accepted; legacy stop() returns at once; the ended monitor still terminates and reaps its child
start_after_a_crash_with_a_held_reader_waits_for_cleanup | regression | SCL-S2.2 | after a crash leaves its output held and the budget is spent, a Start spawns nothing until cleanup
start_after_health_failures_with_a_held_reader_waits_for_cleanup | regression | SCL-S2.2 | after health failures exhaust the budget with output held, a Start spawns nothing until cleanup
start_after_shutdown_is_rejected_closing | regression | SCL-S2.2 | a Start after shutdown begins is RejectedClosing and spawns nothing
late_spawn_after_stop_goes_straight_to_teardown | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a spawn admitted before Stop is torn down unpublished; the Stop stays Pending until the ticket resolves (INV-12)
a_start_racing_the_failed_transition_is_a_fresh_intent | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a Start landing during the Failed transition is a fresh intent, never a join of the failing one
a_start_overtaken_during_its_spawn_reads_superseded | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a Start overtaken by Stop during its spawn reads Superseded, never Started
late_spawn_after_shutdown_is_torn_down | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a spawn admitted before shutdown is torn down; no Start after Closing
publication_ticket_released_before_stop_settles_is_in_the_complete_scope | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a publication admitted before Stop cannot become active after it; its cleanup is in the Complete scope
publication_released_after_the_readers_end_is_in_the_complete_scope | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a ticket released at the settle gate, after the readers end, is waited for: Complete naming publication:<name>
held_publication_ticket_makes_stop_incomplete_until_released | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a held publication ticket makes Stop Incomplete and Quarantined until released
a_dropped_stale_ticket_keeps_the_stop_open | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a stale ticket dropped without cleaned() keeps its publication owned: the Stop is Incomplete naming it and the service stays Quarantined
a_ticket_dropped_by_an_unwinding_caller_keeps_the_stop_open | regression | SCL-S2.3 | an uncommitted ticket dropped by an unwinding caller stays owned: the Stop is Incomplete naming it and the service stays Quarantined
a_withdrawn_ticket_lets_the_stop_complete | positive-control | SCL-S2.3 | a ticket withdrawn before the Stop is resolved and the Stop settles Complete
a_ticket_from_a_replaced_intent_never_becomes_active | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a ticket whose intent a Stop and then a Start replaced is refused as stale, though the service is meant to run again
start_during_teardown_waits_for_an_old_publication_ticket | regression | SCL-S2.3 | a Start superseding a Stop spawns nothing while an old-intent publication ticket is held
shutdown_with_an_open_publication_ticket_is_incomplete | regression | SCL-S2.3 | Stop plus immediate shutdown with an open ticket is Incomplete and stays Quarantined; a late release reconciles
after_shutdown_quarantine_clears_once_readers_and_tickets_are_done | regression | SCL-S2.3 | after shutdown, releasing the last ticket re-checks the readers and reconciles to Stopped
after_shutdown_a_late_reader_end_clears_quarantine | regression | SCL-S2.3 | after shutdown, a late reader end is observed by a snapshot read
shutdown_keeps_a_held_ticket_quarantine | regression | SCL-S2.3 | shutdown does not flip a service Quarantined on a held ticket to Stopped
a_deadline_stop_joining_a_plain_stop_applies_the_tighter_deadline | regression | SCL-S2.4 | a deadline Stop joining a pending Stop arms or tightens its deadline
a_deadline_stop_without_a_monitor_holds_no_record | regression | SCL-S2.4 | with the monitor gone, a deadline Stop leaves no overlay record behind
dropping_a_supervisor_frees_its_deadline_records | regression | SCL-S2.4 | dropping a supervisor frees its deadline records
stop_deadline_expires_while_teardown_is_held | regression | SCL-S2.4 | the publisher marks expiry; late completion never turns DeadlineExpired into Complete
receipt_reports_expiry_even_if_the_publisher_never_ran | regression | SCL-S2.4 | a receipt read after the deadline reports expiry without the publisher (RT-16)
stop_settled_before_its_deadline_is_complete | positive-control | SCL-S2.4 | a Stop inside its deadline is Complete and frees its record
an_expired_stop_superseded_before_it_settles_stays_deadline_expired | regression | SCL-S2.4 | a Start that supersedes a Stop already past its deadline leaves that Stop DeadlineExpired
concurrent_deadline_stops_arm_one_record | regression | SCL-S2.4 | concurrent deadline Stops arm one record; a joining call does not restart the deadline
deadline_overlay_is_fixed_and_full_admission_commits_nothing | regression | SCL-S2.4 | the overlay holds DEADLINE_RECORDS records; arming beyond is Busy and commits nothing
expired_stop_followed_by_later_controls_never_reads_complete | regression | SCL-S2.4 | an expired Stop followed by later controls never reads Complete
publisher_creation_failure_leaves_deadline_admission_unavailable | regression | SCL-S2.4 | creation failure: Unavailable, nothing committed, no replacement (RT-16)
publisher_exit_leaves_admission_unavailable_without_replacement | regression | SCL-S2.4 | a publisher that ends leaves admission Unavailable, no replacement (RT-16)
manifest_lists_every_fixture | harness | SCL-S1.3 | this manifest and the suite list the same fixtures
